      "description": "Watch Frosinone vs Juventus highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 23, 2026. The Serie A clash between Frosinone and Juventus promised to be a rigorous test of tactical discipline for both sides. On August 23, 2026 , the atmosphere was charged as the hosts sought to disrupt the rhythm of the Italian giants in a tightly contested encounter. Bremer’s Header Breaks the Deadlock Juventus established their dominance early, controlling the tempo and searching for openings in the Frosinone backline. The breakthrough arrived in the 22nd minute through a brilliantly executed set-piece routine. Douglas Luiz provided the vision with a key pass to Chico Conceição , who delivered an inviting cross from the right. Gleison Bremer rose highest in the box, powering a header home to give the visitors a deserved lead. The goal was a testament to the clinical nature of the Turin side, who effectively silenced the home crowd. As the first half progressed, Frosinone struggled to create clear-cut chances. A rare moment of controversy occurred in the 31st minute when goalkeeper Lorenzo Palmisani was penalized for an 8-second rule violation, gifting Juventus an indirect set-piece opportunity. The half ended with rising tensions, as Romano Schmid received a yellow card for a robust challenge, underlining the physical battle unfolding on the pitch. Late Drama and Woodwork Rescue The second half saw Juventus maintain a lion's share of possession, peaking at 61%, as they looked to manage the game. Tactical substitutions followed, with Edon Zhegrova and Teun Koopmeiners introduced to provide fresh energy. However, the visitors' defensive resolve was tested, leading to bookings for Zeki Çelik and Andrea Cambiaso as they halted dangerous counter-attacks from the home side. Drama reached fever pitch in stoppage time. In the 93rd minute, Frosinone came agonizingly close to an equalizer when Gabriele Calvani connected with a cross, only to see his powerful header crash against the crossbar. Despite the late onslaught and several last-ditch clearances from Pierre Kalulu and Bremer , Juventus held firm. The final whistle blew after nine minutes of added time, confirming a narrow but vital victory for the visitors."
